//? Title: LZ77 greedy sliding-window byte compression
//? Subtitle: Actual candidate comparisons, overlapping copies and the original repeated pangram
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
LZ77 replaces repeated byte runs with backward-copy tuples and optional literal
bytes. We retain the original repeated-pangram fixture, expose the real greedy
search and decoder writes, validate complete token streams before indexing, and
distinguish native token counts from serialized compressed byte size.
)

\toc

> Tiny overlap-capable greedy match

A token(offset,length,next,literal) copies length bytes from offset positions
behind the current output, then appends next only when literal is true. A pure
literal has offset=length=0. A positive-length match requires an available
positive offset. The encoder searches earlier window starts in increasing order,
replacing the best only for a strictly longer match, so equal-length ties keep
the oldest start and largest offset. Its final match can omit the trailing
literal.

For six a bytes, the first token is a literal a. At input position one, the
candidate starting at zero matches all five remaining bytes, giving offset one
and length five without a final literal. Matching may extend into the current
input run; decoding that tuple repeatedly reads bytes it has just produced. The
real encoder trace below retains every actual comparison and emission, rather
than retelling the token stream through a second matcher.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lz77_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/lz77.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::lz77_encode_trace("aaaaaa");
    std::print("| actual token-start index | actual candidate start | actual matched-prefix before " "comparison | actual candidate byte | actual input byte | equal |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | " "---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (auto &c : t.comparisons)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", c.input, c.candidate,
                   c.length, c.left, c.right, c.equal);
    auto &token = t.analysis.tokens.back();
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("literal", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual first emission\nliteral byte{}",
                       unsigned(static_cast<unsigned char>(
                                t.analysis.tokens.front().next)))).node(
        "match", {6, 0},
        std::format("Actual final greedy match\noffset{}, length{}",
                    token.offset, token.length)).node("end", {12, 0},
                                                      std::format(
                                                      "Actual consumed input\n{} of{} bytes",
                                                      t.emissions.back().next,
                                                      t.input.size())).edge(
        "literal", "match").edge("match", "end");
    d.save_svg("build/lz77_tiny.svg");
}
```
