> Original repeated pangram and native tuples

Retain the original89-byte text, “the quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.”
repeated with a space, using window128 and maximum match length64. The native
helper returns exactly those bytes and no trailing newline. The actual encoder
returns33 tuples and the validated decoder reconstructs all89 bytes exactly. The
table prints next as an unsigned byte value and labels whether that field is
present, so embedded NUL literals are never confused with an absent trailing
literal.

The bar chart compares input bytes with native tuple count. These are different
units: a tuple contains offset/length/literal data and the library defines no
packed wire representation, headers or entropy coding. Fewer tuples alone does
not establish a byte compression ratio, and this educational stream is not a
DEFLATE-compatible file format. No external corpus is needed to retain this
exact synthetic fixture.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lz77_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/lz77.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto input = dm::algorithms::lz77_demo_text();
    auto a = dm::algorithms::lz77_encode_analyze(input, 128, 64);
    auto d = dm::algorithms::lz77_decode_analyze(a.tokens);
    std::print("Actual original bytes {}; actual tuples {}; actual exact round trip {}; real candidate " "visits {}; actual compared bytes {}.\n\n| actual tuple index | actual offset | actual " "copied length | actual next byte or ignored placeholder | literal present |\n| ---: | ---: " "| ---: | ---: | --- |\n",
               input.size(), a.tokens.size(), d.data == input,
               a.work.candidates, a.work.comparisons);
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < a.tokens.size(); ++i) {
        auto &t = a.tokens[i];
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", i, t.offset, t.length,
                   unsigned(static_cast<unsigned char>(t.next)), t.literal);
    }
    auto p =
        dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot({double(input.size()),
                                      double(a.tokens.size())},
                                     {"input bytes", "native tuples"},
                                     "actual count", {22, 163, 74});
    p.x_label("quantity with explicitly different units").y_label(
        "actual native count");
    p.title("Original89-byte fixture: tuples are not packed bytes").save_svg(
        "build/lz77_original.svg");
}
```
