> Real decoder reads can overlap newly produced output

Before each copy token, the decoder’s current output must contain the referenced
offset. Copy byte k reads source=start−offset+k and writes position=start+k.
Because offset is positive, every source is earlier than its corresponding
write, including when source is at or beyond the token’s starting output
position. Such a source byte was produced earlier by this same token, so
periodic runs need no pre-existing full-length source block.

For the six-a example, the first copy reads the original literal at position
zero. Four later copies read positions one through four that the token itself
has already emitted. The native byte trace records the actual token id, source
position, output position and unsigned value for every real write; a literal
uses the SIZE_MAX source sentinel. The plot selects real copy records and shows
both actual index sequences.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lz77_overlap.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/lz77.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto tokens = dm::algorithms::lz77_encode("aaaaaa");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::lz77_decode_trace(tokens);
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    std::print("| actual token | actual output position | actual source or SIZE_MAX literal | actual byte " "|\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (auto &b : t.bytes) {
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", b.token, b.position, b.source,
                   b.value);
        if (b.source != SIZE_MAX) {
            x.push_back(b.position);
            y.push_back(b.source);
        }
    }
    std::print("\nActual copied bytes {}; literals {}; actual reads from output produced within the same " "token {}; actual reconstructed text {}.\n",
               t.analysis.copied, t.analysis.literals,
               t.analysis.overlapping_reads, t.analysis.data);
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(x, y, "actual copy read", {37, 99, 235}, 6).line(
        {1, 5}, {1, 1}, "copy-token start", {220, 38, 38}, 2).x_limits(.5, 5.5).y_limits(-.5, 6).title("Actual overlapping decoder reads").x_label("actual output byte position written").y_label("actual source byte position read").save_svg("build/lz77_overlap.svg");
}
```
