> Complete stream guards and actual window costs

The native tuple fields are int, so encoding accepts at most INT_MAX input bytes
and nonnegative window/match limits. Zero window or zero match cap produces only
literals. Complete input/count geometry is checked; actual counters throw rather
than wrapping. Decoder validation inspects every token and computes complete
output size before emitting any byte: negative fields, zero/unavailable match
offsets, nonzero offsets for pure literals and empty nonliteral tokens are
rejected. General match-only tuples may occur before the final tuple when
supplied directly; the encoder itself omits a literal only at its final match.

An optional decoded-output cap is separate from the container’s own limit; zero
disables the optional cap. The complete decoder trace admits token-count plus
decoded-byte-count logical records before copying, with default million cap. The
encoder’s actual trace admits original bytes plus each real comparison,
completed candidate and emission record as the producer reaches it; unknown
future search decisions are not fabricated. Zero disables optional capture
limits. Fields, capacities, returned/runtime output copies and physical bytes
are excluded; complete capture or exception is promised.

This is a naive search, with a conservative O(n*(1+window*(1+max_match)))
encoder bound and O(output bytes+tokens) decoder work. Actual emission skipping
often reduces comparisons substantially. The original fixed byte fixture below
varies only the prescribed window, records actual candidate/comparison counts,
and independently checks each returned stream by native decoding. These
operation counts are not timing measurements or claims that a larger window must
improve every greedy outcome.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lz77_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/lz77.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto input = dm::algorithms::lz77_demo_text();
    std::vector<double> x, y, z;
    std::print("| prescribed window | actual tuples | actual candidate visits | actual byte comparisons | " "exact round trip |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (int window : {0, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128}) {
        auto a = dm::algorithms::lz77_encode_analyze(input, window, 64);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", window, a.tokens.size(),
                   a.work.candidates, a.work.comparisons,
                   dm::algorithms::lz77_decode(a.tokens) == input);
        x.push_back(window);
        y.push_back(a.work.candidates);
        z.push_back(a.work.comparisons);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, y, "candidate starts", {100, 116, 139}, 2).line(
        x, z, "byte comparisons", {37, 99, 235}, 2).title(
        "Original input: actual greedy search work by window").x_label(
        "prescribed maximum offset").y_label("actual selected native operations").save_svg("build/lz77_work.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| prescribed window | actual tuples | actual candidate visits | actual byte comparisons | exact round trip |
| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |
