\caption(Actual candidate and comparison counts across window controls.)
\alttext(All runs use identical original bytes and match cap64; emitted-token skipping and candidate work are measured separately from any packed-byte size or elapsed time.)

> Verification and references

Native tests exhaust all255 binary strings through length seven across four
window sizes and four match caps, comparing native tuples with independent
substring enumeration and verifying every actual comparison, emission, decoder
byte/source and logical capture count. They retain the original89/33 fixture,
real overlap, match-only streams, binary NUL/high bytes, zero settings, complete
malformed-stream guards, exact output/capture limits, empty cases and ownership.
The ten-report batch passes 95 CTest cases, 30 directly instrumented ASan/UBSan
cases, 121 compiled and executed public examples, 601/601 scoped documentation
definitions and 11 representative hovers. Independent integer, Fraction, graph,
string and NumPy references verify 82,729 records, including the complete
original seeded LSH study. Frozen comparisons preserve ordinary legacy results;
malformed-input, sentinel-collision, ownership and explicit-budget corrections
are documented above. Thirteen checkout headers and thirteen installed headers
compile independently, and an installed-header native consumer links and runs.
Each complete report program runs against the checkout library; all four native
figures are reviewed and HTML/Markdown exports preserve computed results and
image bytes. Batch receipts: `build/mepml-conversion/batch-214-223/`.

J. Ziv and A. Lempel(1977),
[A Universal Algorithm for Sequential Data Compression|https://doi.org/10.1109/TIT.1977.1055714],
IEEE Transactions on Information Theory23(3),337–343. The report illustrates the
sliding-window backward-reference family with this concrete greedy tuple format,
not a standardized packed compressor or an asymptotic code-length theorem for
its unencoded C++ objects.
